```

In this function, we first check if the exponent (m) is 0, in which case we return 1 as any number to the power of 0 is 1. If the exponent is negative, we call the same function but with the negative of the exponent and then return the reciprocal of the result, effectively handling the case of negative exponents. On the other hand, if the exponent is positive, then we perform the multiplication using the base (n) and call the same function with an exponent of (m - 1). This will continue until m is 0, at which point it will stop the recursion and return the result.

