The provided C++ script is already optimized to display the first 50 Fibonacci numbers. However, due to the limitation on the maximum value an unsigned long long can store in C++ (18,446,744,073,709,551,615), the program can only correctly calculate up to the 93rd Fibonacci number. After that, it will start to overflow and produce wrong results.

Below is the improved version that adds comments for readability, and includes the handling of overflow issue:

```cpp
#include <iostream>

