This code first gets user's string input, then it iterates through the string character by character. `isdigit()` is used to check if a character is a digit. If the character is a digit, it's appended to a digit string. `isalpha()` is used to check if a character is an alphabet. If the character is an alphabet, it's appended to an alphabet string. Finally, the digit and alphabet strings are printed.

Please note that this program can work only with one word strings. If you enter multiple words separated by space, the program will consider only the first word as input string.

