1. In chrome browser, I am using MacBook to record a 30 minutes class, in code, use getDisplayMedia to get the screen stream：



navigator.mediaDevices.getDisplayMedia({audio:true,video:true}).then((mediaStream)=>{
     mediaRecorder = new MediaRecorder(mediaStream,{mineType:'video/webm'})
   })


2.When the recording started 5 minutes later, I connected an external microphone to the MacBook, then lectured through the microphone, and then hoped that my voice would be recorded through the microphone, but the strange thing is that since the microphone is connected, there is no recording screen behind The sound is down, what’s the matter, how can I operate so that I can continue recording when switching microphones?

The main reason behind this issue is that `getDisplayMedia` does not automatically switch to a new input like an external microphone. When you start recording, `getDisplayMedia` will use the default input source available at that time.

So if you connect a new microphone later, it will not be used because at the time of recording it is not the default input source.

To overcome this issue, what you can do is pause the recording, switch inputs, and then continue recording.

Another solution could be stopping the recording, starting a new recording with the new media device that was recently connected and finally, merging the two videos. Currently, there is no API that enables realtime switching of the MediaDevices.

Consider using `ondevicechange` event of `MediaDevices` to get to know when the user plugs in a new microphone, then you can stop the current stream, and restart it with the new microphone.

Here is an example: 

```
navigator.mediaDevices.ondevicechange = function(event) {
  // enumerate devices...
  navigator.mediaDevices.enumerateDevices()
   .then(function(devices) {
     devices.forEach(function(device) {
       if (device.kind === 'audioinput') {
         // Stop the current stream
         mediaStream.getTracks().forEach(track => track.stop());

         // Start a new stream with the new device
         var constraints = {audio: {deviceId: device.deviceId}, video: true};
         navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia(constraints).then(function(newStream) {
           mediaRecorder = new MediaRecorder(newStream, {mineType: 'video/webm'});
           // call methods to play or record the new stream...
         });
       }
     });
   })
   .catch(function(err) {
     console.log(err.name + ": " + err.message);
   });
};
```

This way, whenever a new microphone is connected to the MacBook, the earlier screen capture stream is stopped and a new stream is started with the newly connected device.

