To obtain a nested field from the Protocol Buffers (protobuf) message, you would need to navigate through the fields similar to accessing the properties of a nested object. However, Protobuf doesn't allow direct access to fields via a string path ("person_data.first_name") out of the box.

Here's a generalized way you can access nested fields, it involves splitting the string and accessing nested fields one by one.

```java
public Object getFieldValueFromPath(Message message, String path){
    String[] pathElements = path.split("\\.");
    FieldDescriptor fd = null;
    for(String element : pathElements){
        fd = message.getDescriptorForType().findFieldByName(element);
        if(fd == null) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Field '" + element + "' not found in " + message.getDescriptorForType().getName() + ".");
        }

        if(fd.getType() == FieldDescriptor.Type.MESSAGE){
            message = (Message) message.getField(fd);
        } else {
            return message.getField(fd);
        }
    }
    return null;
}
```
