Here is a JavaScript code snippet that computes the prime factors of a given integer.

```javascript
function primeFactors(n){
    var factors = [], 
        divisor = 2;

    while(n > 2){
        if(n % divisor == 0){
           factors.push(divisor); 
           n = n / divisor;
        }
        else{
          divisor++;
        }      
    }
    return factors;
}

console.log(primeFactors(12)); // outputs: [2, 2, 3]
```

This code sets a divisor equal to 2 and repeatedly checks if the input number can be divided by the divisor. If it can, the divisor is added to the list of prime factors and the original number is divided by the divisor. If the input number can't be divided by the divisor the divisor is incremented.

Finally, the list of prime factors is returned. For example, for the input of n = 12, the code will return [2, 2, 3].
